Copyright (c) 2026 [Licensor]

1. What this license covers

This license covers the files in the "ee/" directory of the OwnBase
repository and any changes made to them (together, "the Software").
Everything outside "ee/" is licensed separately, under the MIT license in
the LICENSE file at the root of the repository, unless a file says
otherwise.

2. Developing and testing

You may copy, change and run the Software to develop and test it, and to
develop and test your own use of OwnBase, without a subscription or a
license key.

3. Production use

You may use the Software in production only if you, and any organisation
you act for, have a valid OwnBase Enterprise subscription and license key
for at least the number of members you use it with, and keep to the
subscription terms agreed with [Licensor]. "Production" means any use other
than the developing and testing allowed in section 2.

4. Changes

You may change the Software and publish your changes as patches. [Licensor]
and its licensors keep all right, title and interest in the Software and
in changes to it. Changed Software may be used in production only as
section 3 allows.

5. What is not allowed

Except as this license allows, you may not copy, merge, publish,
distribute, sublicense or sell the Software. You may not remove, disable,
change or get around the license key checks, or the notices they show, or
make the Software's features work without a valid license key.

6. Other people's components

Components by others that are part of the Software stay under their own
licenses.

7. No warranty, no liability

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING
FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER
